        ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x+1}$, find ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$\n\n${f}^{\u2032}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=x+1,$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{\u2032}(x) & =2x, \\\\ {v}^{\u2032}(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{\u2032}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\cdot (x+1)-{x}^{2}\\cdot 1}{{(x+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+2x-{x}^{2}}{{(x+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x}{(x+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
